# Delivery — README, Setup & Submission

For the full workflow and README template, use the `delivery-and-readme` skill.

## Runnable cold
- Reviewers "run it cold". The project must start via `docker-compose up` or a simple
  setup script, and setup must work in under 5 minutes.
- `docker-compose.yml` at the root spins up backend + frontend together.
- Database migrations must be applied as part of setup — no manual hidden steps.

## Environment files
- `backend/.env.example` contains at least: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`,
  `DATABASE_URL`, `FLASK_ENV`, `SECRET_KEY` — placeholder values only.
- `frontend/src/environments/environment.ts` has `production: false` and
  `apiUrl: 'http://localhost:5000'`; `environment.prod.ts` exists.
- `.env` is git-ignored. Never commit real keys.

## README must cover (each one is graded or required)
- Setup for BOTH backend and frontend, step by step.
- Architecture overview.
- Agent design (three agents, orchestrator, partial-failure handling, validation/fallback).
- Opportunity score formula with explanation.
- Tradeoffs and design decisions (including every resolved spec gap).
- AI model selection (OpenAI GPT-4o or Anthropic Claude) and why.
- AI coding tools used and for what.
- Frontend install/serve instructions (spec: "ng install && ng serve").

## Dependencies
- Pin backend dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`; frontend deps in `package.json`.
- Only add dependencies required by the spec or confirmed by the user.

## Submission
- Push to a public or private GitHub repository; if private, invite the hiring manager.
- Submit the repository link via the portal or email provided.
